Corpus provenance
=================

benign/
  Real AUR PKGBUILDs, copied verbatim from the AUR git repositories at the
  revision recorded in each case's CASE file (`revision=`). They are published
  under the terms of their respective upstream projects; they are vendored here
  so the detector can be tested offline and so a false-positive regression is
  caught in CI rather than by a user. No modification is made to their content.

malicious/
  Synthetic and incident-derived samples. Each CASE file records the incident
  the sample is modelled on. Command-and-control hosts are rewritten to
  reserved example domains (c2.example): the detectors match shape, not host,
  and no live payload endpoint is stored here.

To add a benign case from a local AUR helper cache:

  d=~/.cache/paru/clone/<pkg>
  mkdir -p tests/corpus/benign/<pkg>
  cp "$d/PKGBUILD" tests/corpus/benign/<pkg>/
  cp "$d"/*.install tests/corpus/benign/<pkg>/ 2>/dev/null
  printf 'max_tier=ok\nnote=<why this package is interesting>\nrevision=%s\n' \
    "$(git -C "$d" rev-parse HEAD)" > tests/corpus/benign/<pkg>/CASE
